# Terraform credentials and settings for envs/prod, as 1Password secret
# references. Run Terraform from this directory under `op run`, which swaps each
# op:// reference for its value in the owner's 1Password vault for that one
# process:
#
#   op run --env-file=1password.env -- terraform plan
#
# Nothing here is a secret, and nothing is written to disk. No .tfvars file is
# needed: a terraform.tfvars or *.auto.tfvars left in this directory would
# override these TF_VAR_* values. infra/README.md lists the items and fields.
#
# hcp-terraform (Development vault), referenced by its item ID: the HCP Terraform
# user API token and organization name, the same item the chronos repository uses.
TF_TOKEN_app_terraform_io="op://Development/snuoe5g63q73gugkpj3z256i4q/credential"
TF_CLOUD_ORGANIZATION="op://Development/snuoe5g63q73gugkpj3z256i4q/organization"
# cloudflare-terraform (Development vault): the Cloudflare API token that the
# chronos repository's Terraform uses too, also allowed on the anisotro.pics zone
# (permissions in infra/README.md), and the account ID.
TF_VAR_cloudflare_api_token="op://Development/cloudflare-terraform/credential"
TF_VAR_cloudflare_account_id="op://Development/cloudflare-terraform/account-id"
